      "message": "Just a drive by thought, but if we have additional declared functions for each runtime effect, we can implement this general `GetKnownRuntimeEffect(key)` and have the effect-specific code define the particular `GetKnownRuntimeEffect` function, e.g `GetBlurRuntimeEffect4()`.\n\nWith the image filter shaders, there are a lot of details coupled between the C++ code and the SkSL and it\u0027s nice to have them defined next to one another. It\u0027s somewhat similar to the distance issue created between RenderSteps and their functions being defined in modules, but then we get the added benefit of pre-compilation and minification.\n\nThat makes me wonder if we can actually move the meat of these known shader codes to a module that\u0027s visible to all backends, and then we link the stable key with the function name and signature?",
